<StandardPageLayout title="Privacy" headline="Privacy" description="How TheAngrySquirrel handles comments, security checks, and third-party media.">
  <p>Updated November 4, 2026.</p>
  <p>TheAngrySquirrel is Patrick Rich’s professional portfolio and personal journal.</p>
  <h2>Comments</h2>
  <p>If you submit a comment, the site stores your chosen name, comment, submission time, moderation status, and any reply relationship in Cloudflare D1. Approved names and comments become public. No reader account or email address is required. Do not include information you do not want published.</p>
  <p>Comments are reviewed before publication. To request removal of a comment, contact <a href="mailto:patrickprich@angrysquirrel.org">patrickprich@angrysquirrel.org</a> with the article and comment details.</p>
  <h2>Security and spam prevention</h2>
  <p>Cloudflare delivers and protects the site and may process technical information such as your IP address, browser information, and security cookies. Comment submission uses Cloudflare Turnstile. The comment system uses a daily keyed hash derived from your IP address for rate limiting, rather than storing the raw IP address in the comments database. This does not describe Cloudflare’s separate security logs.</p>
  <p>See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a> for its processing practices.</p>
  <h2>Images, video, and external links</h2>
  <p>Some pages load images from external providers and embed YouTube or Vimeo video. Loading these resources sends requests to those providers, which may process your IP address and browser information under their own policies. YouTube embeds use its privacy-enhanced domain. Links below videos offer another way to open them if embedded playback is unavailable.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this site or its privacy practices can be sent to <a href="mailto:patrickprich@angrysquirrel.org">patrickprich@angrysquirrel.org</a>.</p>
</StandardPageLayout>
